// The guest seat's demo (`demo=guest`, 2026-10-25): you are a rove beetle
// that lives off an ant colony by smelling like it. The design and its two
// reviews are `Reports/guest-seat-demo-2026-10-25.md`.
//
// **Steady income's box and colony, landed early.** The beggar needs a
// grown nest with brood and fed workers to beg from, which steady income
// grows by about frame 30,000 (`examples/guestprobe.rs` DONORS: adults
// there hold 2-5 grants). The colony lands at 600 rather than 6,000 so the
// warm-up is shorter; the seat runs the clock at top speed until the
// guest lands (`land=`, default 30,000) and then drops to 1x. Nothing else
// differs from steady_income, so a guest's cost reads against that box.
(
    name: "demo_guest",
    title: "GUEST",
    question: "You are a rove beetle at an ant nest. Smell like family and they feed you; smell wrong and they bite. How long can you live off them?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [
        (subject: "the bed", field: "rain", value: 0),
    ],
    placements: [],
    timeline: [
        (at: 600, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
        (at: 600, every: 1000, until: 0, what: Heap(material: "provisions", x: 286, cells: 40)),
    ],
    horizon: 600000,
)
